105: ## Repo layout
106: 
107: - `.dhall/` — crew + agent definitions (Dhall; the single source of truth)
108: - `worker/worker.py` — the MQTT worker each role runs
109: - `sut-setup/` — TF that configures the host systems (services)
110: - `hosts/`, `modules/` — optional NixOS config for the broker host
111: - `flake.nix` — the `nix develop` shell (nixpkgs as flake input, containing Agda + dependencies)
112: - `Makefile` — compiles the crews (`make`)
113: - `resources/` — papers, `knowledge/`, `skills/` the agents use
114: 
115: ## Requirements
116: 
117: - Three Raspberry Pis running **Raspberry Pi OS (Any Linux with Systemd, aarch64)**
118: - The **Nix package manager** (nixpkgs provides every tool; see above —
119:   NixOS is *not* required)
120: - One host system (x86_64 Linux) featuring an **8GB GPU and 16GB RAM** for the SUT + MQTT broker + local model server, set up with TF (`sut-setup/`)
121: - A local web server to test, reachable from every Pi (the TF setup
122:   deploys Juice Shop for us): https://owasp.org
