132: ## Host systems via Terraform/OpenTofu 
133: 
134: The host machines (SUT + MQTT broker + Grafana) are **configured with
135: TF**, not hand-edited. `terraform` ships in `nix develop`.
136: 
137: ```sh
138: cd sut-setup
139: terraform init
140: terraform apply
141: ```
142: 
143: This installs podman, writes the Quadlet unit files and starts a pod with
144: 
145: - **EMQX** — the MQTT broker (1883 MQTT, 8083 WebSocket, 18083 dashboard)
146: - **Juice Shop** — the system under test (OWASP project)
147: - **Grafana** — metrics/dashboard
148: - **nginx** — reverse proxy on :80
149: 
150: Services bind to `0.0.0.0` by default so the Pis can reach them over the LAN;
151: tune `bind_address` / `expose_public` in `sut-setup/variables.tf`. Tear down
152: with `systemctl --user stop <service>` then `tofu destroy`. Details in
153: `sut-setup/README.md`.
154: 
155: ## Managing the Compute Server (GPU / models / database / Agda)
156: 
157: The nixpkgs-hosted tooling lets you manage this backend architecture uniformly (or lock it down on NixOS via the optional `broker` deployment in `flake.nix`). The 4-bit quantized model and the Agda service share this node's system memory footprint seamlessly via isolated process parameters.
