## mosquitto 2.1.2 (`eclipse-mosquitto:2`) — all verified by experiment

- `allow_anonymous` / `password_file` are **per listener**. Do not emit
  `per_listener_settings`; it is deprecated and warns.
- `acl_file` is **global** — it constrains the loopback listener too. Consequence:
  with an acl_file present, anonymous clients may subscribe but **every publish is
  denied**, so an anonymous round-trip probe is impossible. Hence the dedicated
  `healthcheck` account confined to `healthcheck/#`.
- Config **comments must be flush-left**. An indented `#` is parsed as a
  directive: `Error: Unknown configuration variable '#'.`
- The container runs as uid/gid **1883** and its entrypoint chowns only
  `/mosquitto/data`. So: anything else it reads must be world-readable (hence
  0644 on `passwd`/`acl`; mosquitto 2.1.2 only warns but 3.0 plans to refuse), and
  `log_dest file` into a host-owned dir fails — use `log_dest stdout`.
- **The image has no bash**, so no `/dev/tcp`. It does have `nc`, `mosquitto_sub`,
  `mosquitto_pub`. Its `/bin/sh` is busybox: **no brace expansion** (`cp a/{b,c}` fails).
- `mosquitto_pub` **exits 0 even when the broker denies the publish** — MQTT 3.1.1
